        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger de Bankwell, Edward I of England\n- Publications: Year Books\n- Roles: counsel, Scottish king\n- Topics: regnal years, epithets\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1340 Year Books publication, Roger de Bankwell appears as a counsel.\n- The first reign included in that 1340 publication was that of a king described as the Scottish king.\n- Edward I of England was also known as Edward Longshanks and the Hammer of the Scots.\n- The Scottish king whose reign was the first included in the 1340 publication was Edward I of England.",
